##DESCRIPTION
## MAT237 M2 Q6
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('multivariable calculus','fundamental theorems','flux','divergence')

## DBsubject('Multivariable Calculus')
## DBchapter('Vector calculus')
## DBsection('Divergence theorem')
## Institution('University of Toronto')
## Section1('M2')
## Problem1('6')


########################################################################

DOCUMENT();      

loadMacros(
   "PGstandard.pl",     # Standard macros for PG language
   "MathObjects.pl",
   #"source.pl",        # allows code to be displayed on certain sites.
   #"PGcourse.pl",      # Customization file for the course
);

# Print problem number and point value (weight) for the problem
TEXT(beginproblem());

# Show which answers are correct and which ones are incorrect
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

##############################################################
#
#  Setup
#
#
Context("Numeric");

$q1 = Compute("2pi"); #M2 Q6.1
$q2 = Compute("4pi(237^3-137^3)"); #M2 Q6.2


##############################################################
#
#  Text
#
#

Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_TEXT
Armed with the divergence theorem, you can revisit some nasty flux computations. $BR

1. Use the divergence theorem to compute the outward flux of \( F(x,y,z) = (x^3,x+y^3,3z-2) \) through the boundary of the solid paraboloid \( R = \lbrace (x,y,z) \in \mathbb{R}^3 : x^2+y^2 \leq z \leq 1 \rbrace. \) You may give a decimal answer rounded to two decimal places or an exact value. $BR

\{$q1->ans_rule\}
$BR 
2. Use the divergence theorem to compute the outward flux of \( F(x,y,z) = (x,y,z) \) through the boundary of the solid hollowed out ball \( \lbrace (x,y,z) \in \mathbb{R}^3 : 137^2 \leq x^2+y^2+z^2 \leq 237^2 \rbrace. \) You may give an exact value or round to the nearest whole number $BR

\{$q2->ans_rule\}
END_TEXT
Context()->normalStrings;

##############################################################
#
#  Answers
#
#

ANS($q1->with(tolerance=>.01)->cmp);
ANS($q2->with(tolerance=>.01)->cmp);

# default tolerance is .01 or one percent.


ENDDOCUMENT();